# RTL kernels' memory arguments, by example (prep_cfg.py only reads HLS C/C++ sources, so an RTL kernel's m_axi ports
# were never pinned and v++ put them on the platform's default memory -- HOST on route V, where the kernels then wrote
# nowhere the host reads: rtl_adder_streams / rtl_vadd_2clks "Result mismatch, Device result = 0" on hpz440, 2026-10-08).
# Derived from each xclbin's EMBEDDED_METADATA (arg names) + CONNECTIVITY. Pinned to VMEM's first memory.
# example            cu.arg
rtl_adder_streams    krnl_input_stage_rtl_1.input_r
rtl_adder_streams    krnl_output_stage_rtl_1.output_r
rtl_vadd_2clks       krnl_vadd_2clk_rtl_1.a
rtl_vadd_2clks       krnl_vadd_2clk_rtl_1.b
rtl_vadd_2clks       krnl_vadd_2clk_rtl_1.c
rtl_vadd_2kernels    krnl_vadd_rtl_0_1.a
rtl_vadd_2kernels    krnl_vadd_rtl_0_1.b
rtl_vadd_2kernels    krnl_vadd_rtl_0_1.c
rtl_vadd_2kernels    krnl_vadd_rtl_1_1.a
rtl_vadd_2kernels    krnl_vadd_rtl_1_1.b
rtl_vadd_2kernels    krnl_vadd_rtl_1_1.c
rtl_vadd_hw_debug    krnl_vadd_rtl_1.a
rtl_vadd_hw_debug    krnl_vadd_rtl_1.b
rtl_vadd_hw_debug    krnl_vadd_rtl_1.c
